// Text helpers (lib/string.tersus) and the connectives `&&`, `||` and `!`. `String::fromInt(n)` is the decimal text of an Int, `s.find(b, from)` the index of the first
// Byte b at or after an index (the size of the string when there is none), `s.slice(from, to)` the bytes between two indexes and `s.startsWith(prefix)` whether it starts
// with another string. `a && b` does not evaluate b when a is false, and the validator knows a when it checks b: the slices below are in range because the test
// that `=` was found came first.

line = "width=".concat(String::fromInt(0 - 120));
equals = line.find(toByte(61), 0);
affirm equals >= 0 && equals <= size(line);

if equals < size(line) && line.startsWith("width") {
    key = line.slice(0, equals);
    value = line.slice(equals + 1, size(line));
    key.print();
    writeByte(10);
    value.print();
    writeByte(10);
    return size(key) * 100 + size(value);
};
return 0;
